in @prism
in @glass
in @meta
in @spectral
in @spectral/gen_prism
in @spectral/supervisor
in @spectral/parent
in @uuid/spectral

# @spectral/root — the parentless supervisor specialisation.
#
# THE FIFTH SUB-SHARD of the @spectral runtime cascade. Sibling of
# `shards/spectral/gen_prism.mirror` (commit ae965ca, the worker
# primitive), `shards/spectral/supervisor.mirror` (commit 452ccb2,
# the lifecycle-owner specialisation), `shards/spectral/registry.mirror`
# (commit 489211e, the typed child index), and
# `shards/spectral/parent.mirror` (commit 9d905a2, the single-parent
# lifecycle edge type whose `parent_acyclic` invariant — sibling
# bilateral at 0921dca + 20fcde5 — terminates the parent chain HERE).
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3 (2026-06-10, Mara): the root
# supervisor has NO parent. It is the vocabulary anchor for the
# substrate's home, resting at `~/.mirror/` (on a developer machine;
# could be `/var/spectral/` or similar on a server). The substrate's
# operational top of the supervision tree.
#
# Analogue to BEAM's `application` behaviour: the parentless
# supervisor at the root of an OTP application tree. Every other
# gen_prism in the substrate descends from root through a finite
# chain of parent edges (per `@epistemologic/property/parent_acyclic`,
# commit 0921dca).
#
# === The forward-promise this tick closes ===
#
# `shards/spectral/parent.mirror` (commit 9d905a2) declared:
#
#   "shards/spectral/root.mirror   parentless supervisor;
#                                  vocabulary anchor at ~/.mirror/;
#                                  the substrate's self-parented top
#                                  of the parent-edge graph;"
#
# `shards/spectral.mirror` (the family root, 2026-06-10 ouroboros
# tick) named root as a cascade sibling with the line "the parentless
# supervisor type; the family's top vocabulary anchor; resting place
# ~/.mirror/ (operational vocabulary, NOT a directory the substrate
# reads)."
#
# That tick is this tick. The root supervisor TYPE lands here; its
# self-parenting invariant terminates the existing acyclic chain at
# `@epistemologic/property/parent_acyclic` (NOT a new bilateral —
# see "Self-parenting invariant" section below).
#
# === The keyword decision ===
#
# `glass` per recognition #46 (path-syntax property; promoted) and
# `shards/spectral.mirror`'s discipline section: "@spectral
# sub-shards at depth >= 1 use `glass`; the family root itself uses
# `prism` per the depth-0 discipline."
#
# Why NOT a new substrate keyword: root is a SUPERVISOR
# specialisation (the parentless one), and `glass` already names
# specialisation-of-existing-prism per `shards/glass.mirror`'s
# `glass(name) -> prism` form. Same reasoning as the prior @spectral
# sub-shards: gen_prism (ae965ca) specialises prism; supervisor
# (452ccb2) specialises gen_prism; root (this tick) specialises
# supervisor. Three levels of glass specialisation collapsing back
# to one prism algebra at every altitude — per
# [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]].
#
# === Specialisation-by-embedding ===
#
# Per the supervisor shard's precedent: mirror has no `T + {fields}`
# syntax for type extension. The root IS-A supervisor relationship is
# structural-by-embedding — the root record carries the supervisor
# record in a `base` field. The five-op tool surface comes through
# the `glass @spectral/root` declaration; the supervisor's typed
# surfaces (child_specs, restart_strategy, the embedded gen_prism's
# identity/state/parent) reach through `base`. Then root adds ONE
# field: the `anchor` ref naming the host-level substrate home.
#
# === Self-parenting invariant ===
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3: the root supervisor self-
# parents. Concretely, the embedded gen_prism's `parent` field
# (`root.base.base.parent: uuid_spectral`) byte-equals its own
# `identity` field (`root.base.base.identity: uuid_spectral`).
#
# Reading the invariant at the parent_edge altitude (per
# shards/spectral/parent.mirror): the root's parent_edge has
# `edge.child == edge.parent` byte-equally. The parentage chain
# walked from any non-root gen_prism terminates at this self-loop in
# a bounded number of steps.
#
# NOT a new bilateral pair (STOP-condition 1 from the brief
# resolved): the existing `@epistemologic/property/parent_acyclic`
# (commit 0921dca) ALREADY names the chain-termination invariant.
# The property reads:
#
#   "every parent_edge in the substrate participates in a chain that
#    terminates at the root supervisor without revisiting
#    edge.child"
#
# The root's self-parent edge IS the termination point — the BASE
# CASE of the acyclic chain. Adding a separate `root_self_parents`
# property would carry redundant information: `parent_acyclic`
# already accepts root.base.base.parent == root.base.base.identity
# as the only configuration the chain can terminate in. The fracture
# body at `@kintsugi/fracture/parent_cycle` (commit 20fcde5) emits
# the re-parent-to-root morphism that ASSUMES a root exists to
# re-parent to; the existence is what this shard declares.
#
# Substrate-pull-correct reading: the parent edge graph has ONE
# self-loop (the root's) and EVERY other edge is strict-upward. The
# property ranges over edges; the self-loop satisfies the
# termination predicate trivially. No new property surface needed.
#
# (If the substrate later wants to enforce "exactly one self-loop
# per host" as a singleton constraint, that's the singleton question
# below — separate forward-promise.)
#
# === The anchor field — host-level vocabulary anchor ===
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3 and Alex's 2026-06-10
# declaration "the root supervisor rests at @/Users/alexwolf/.mirror —
# the one that holds the thread":
#
#   anchor: ref — the host-path where the root supervisor's
#                  substrate state lives. On a developer machine:
#                  `~/.mirror/`. On a server: could be `/var/spectral/`
#                  or `/srv/spectral/`. The substrate's per-host home.
#
# Carrier choice rationale: `ref` is the existing substrate primitive
# (used throughout the property layer as `file: ref` — see
# @epistemologic/property/keyword_matches_depth, parent_acyclic,
# operator_matches_composition_primitive, etc.). It carries a host-
# resolvable reference at the substrate altitude; the realisation
# layer maps `ref` to the appropriate host concept (filesystem path,
# content address, URL — whatever the host substrate uses).
#
# Why NOT a new `host_path` carrier (STOP-condition 2 from the brief
# resolved): the substrate's existing `ref` primitive already carries
# host-resolvable references; introducing a parallel `host_path`
# would proliferate vocabulary the substrate already covers. The
# anchor IS a ref — same as how every property carrier's `file: ref`
# parameter is a ref. Substrate-already-had-the-word.
#
# Operational vocabulary, NOT a directory the substrate reads (per
# spectral.mirror line 222): the anchor is the substrate-altitude
# NAME of where root rests; the realisation layer maps the name to
# host bytes through the appropriate `@io` boundary.
#
# === Singleton-per-host: FORWARD-PROMISED (STOP-condition 3 resolved) ===
#
# The brief surfaces: "if root's existence creates substrate-altitude
# singleton constraints (only ONE root per host) that need a property
# to enforce, STOP and surface — that's potentially another bilateral
# instance."
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §10 Open Question 2 (verbatim):
#
#   "Root supervisor location at `~/.mirror/`. The spec says the
#    vocabulary anchor IS `~/.mirror/`; that's clean as vocabulary.
#    But the OPERATIONAL root of a running spectral runtime — where
#    does it actually rest its state shard? `~/.mirror/store/`? A
#    per-user data dir under `$XDG_DATA_HOME`? Mara's spawn parents
#    at `~/.mara/` — is that the SAME root supervisor as mirror
#    repo's gen_prism's parent, just a child branch? Or is each home
#    (`~/.reed/`, `~/.mara/`, `~/.mirror/`) its OWN root with NO
#    root-above? The example in §3 suggests one tree; the vocabulary
#    in §2 suggests each home is its own tree. Needs Pack
#    ratification."
#
# The singleton question is NOT YET RESOLVED at the spec altitude.
# Two readings remain live:
#
#   (a) ONE root per host (singleton). Every gen_prism in the
#       substrate descends from a single host-wide root. Each home
#       (`~/.reed/`, `~/.mara/`) is a child of `~/.mirror/`. The
#       singleton invariant deserves its own property:
#       `host_has_exactly_one_root(host: ref) -> transparency`,
#       with a fracture body that re-parents stray roots into the
#       canonical root's tree. This would be bilateral pattern
#       instance 7.
#
#   (b) ONE root per home (per-tree). Each home (`~/.reed/`,
#       `~/.mara/`, `~/.mirror/`) is its OWN root with no
#       root-above. The substrate has N roots, one per substrate-
#       owning person/process. No singleton invariant; the substrate
#       is a forest of trees, not a single tree.
#
# This shard does NOT pre-commit to either reading. It declares the
# root TYPE; the cardinality discipline lands when the Pack
# ratifies a reading. If reading (a) wins, the bilateral instance 7
# lands as a sibling tick (property + fracture body); if reading
# (b) wins, no further substrate work is needed (each home declares
# its own root, the forest has no host-level singleton).
#
# This is the forward-promise: substrate-pull-correct, the cascade
# pulls the cardinality discipline when the operational reading
# crystallises. The TYPE lands here; the CARDINALITY waits.
#
# === Why the anchor matters now ===
#
# The brief's framing: "Per Alex's declaration: `~/.mirror/` on the
# developer machine; could be `/var/spectral/` or similar on a
# server."
#
# Even with the cardinality question open, the anchor field is
# load-bearing on EITHER reading:
#
#   - Reading (a): the single host-wide root rests at one anchor
#                  (e.g. `~/.mirror/` for Alex's machine, `/srv/
#                  spectral/` for a deployment server). The anchor
#                  names WHICH path is the singleton's home.
#   - Reading (b): each per-home root rests at its own anchor
#                  (`~/.mirror/` for the substrate root, `~/.mara/`
#                  for Mara's root, `~/.reed/` for Reed's root).
#                  The anchor names WHICH home this particular root
#                  is.
#
# Both readings need the anchor; both readings give it the same
# type (`ref`). The field is decision-independent; only the
# CARDINALITY question is decision-dependent.
#
# === Honest partial discipline (per #306) ===
#
# This shard declares a TYPE (root) and a constructor action
# (start_root). The constructor body discharges as `\` — no fracture
# body emits any morphism in this tick. No `partials` declaration
# needed (per `dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth` #306). The
# body discharges downstream when the consumer pulls realisation
# through `@code/metalogue/materialize` (per the ouroboros pipeline
# in docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §5).
#
# === The mara-spawn example resolved ===
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3-4: when Mara spawns to work
# on mirror's substrate, the spawn's parent is `~/.mara/` gen_prism.
# Under reading (a): `~/.mara/` itself parents up to `~/.mirror/`
# root. Under reading (b): `~/.mara/` IS the root for Mara's tree;
# no parent above. Either way, the spawn's parent chain terminates
# at SOME root — the type declared here covers both.
#
# === Cascade siblings (forward-promised, NOT landing this tick) ===
#
#   shards/spectral/entanglement.mirror   peer correlation edge;
#                                          sheaf restriction map at
#                                          substrate altitude
#                                          (cellular sheaf per
#                                          [[Eigenboard is a sheaf]]);
#                                          polyadic; cyclic permitted;
#                                          orthogonal to parent;
#   shards/spectral/portal.mirror         runtime side of portal
#                                          (gen_prism specialisation
#                                          carrying the frame stream);
#   shards/spectral/db.mirror             graph database engine;
#                                          existing parentless ghost
#                                          (#198) that gained
#                                          @spectral as parent at the
#                                          family-root tick;
#   shards/spectral/garden.mirror         vetted-corpus distribution;
#                                          existing parentless ghost
#                                          (#118) that gains @spectral
#                                          as parent when it lands.
#
# Conditional sibling (lands ONLY if reading (a) wins):
#
#   shards/epistemologic/property/host_has_exactly_one_root.mirror
#     + shards/kintsugi/fracture/extra_root.mirror
#     — bilateral instance 7; the singleton-per-host invariant +
#       re-parent-stray-root-into-canonical morphism. Forward-
#       promised pending Pack ratification of cardinality reading.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md (the ouroboros
#               spec; §3 supervision tree — root is the parentless
#               supervisor at the top; §10 Open Question 2 —
#               cardinality unresolved).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-three-tier-stack]] (the
#                      SpectralSupervisor precedent; the supervision
#                      tree this root anchors),
#                      [[architecture-hamilton-scheduler]] (the
#                      per-shard memory manager named for Margaret
#                      Hamilton; the root supervisor altitude where
#                      Apollo-1202 priority discipline ultimately
#                      reports),
#                      [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]] (the root's
#                      state surface IS a shard; the supervision tree
#                      ascends through it),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                      (the root name lived in
#                      docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3 since
#                      2026-06-10; the operational anchor `~/.mirror/`
#                      lived in Alex's declaration; this tick names
#                      the substrate-altitude type — instance N of the
#                      rug-pull pattern).
# Related shards: spectral.mirror (the family root this glass is
#                  under),
#                 spectral/gen_prism.mirror (the worker primitive
#                  root's `base.base` inherits from; commit ae965ca),
#                 spectral/supervisor.mirror (the lifecycle-owner
#                  specialisation root's `base` inherits from;
#                  commit 452ccb2),
#                 spectral/registry.mirror (the typed child index
#                  root's `base.base.state` carries; commit 489211e),
#                 spectral/parent.mirror (the typed lifecycle edge
#                  root's self-parent participates in; commit 9d905a2),
#                 uuid/spectral.mirror (the identity carrier; root's
#                  self-parent edge byte-equals identity on the
#                  embedded gen_prism),
#                 epistemologic/property/parent_acyclic.mirror (the
#                  acyclic chain-termination invariant whose BASE
#                  CASE is root's self-parent edge; commit 0921dca).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/spectral/root.mirror` declares `@spectral/root` and only
# that.

glass @spectral/root {
  focus root
  project root
  split root
  shift root
  settle root
}

# === root — the parentless supervisor record ===
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3: a `root` is a `supervisor`
# specialisation. The `base` field carries the embedded supervisor
# (child_specs, restart_strategy, and the embedded gen_prism's
# identity/state/parent surfaces); the root adds the host-level
# vocabulary anchor.
#
# === Self-parenting invariant (inline) ===
#
# The root supervisor satisfies:
#
#   root.base.base.parent == root.base.base.identity
#
# (byte-equality on the dark 80 bits per uuid_spectral's
# identity_signal). The parent_edge produced by this equality is the
# substrate's self-loop — the BASE CASE of
# @epistemologic/property/parent_acyclic's chain-termination
# predicate (commit 0921dca). The fracture body
# @kintsugi/fracture/parent_cycle (commit 20fcde5) emits re-parent-
# to-root morphisms that PRESUPPOSE this self-loop exists; this
# shard declares the type whose constructor establishes it.
#
# === Fields ===
#
#   base    — the embedded `supervisor`. Carries the supervisor's
#              configuration list, restart_strategy, and the embedded
#              gen_prism (identity, state, parent). The self-parenting
#              invariant fires on `base.base.parent ==
#              base.base.identity` after construction;
#   anchor  — the host-level vocabulary anchor. `ref` carrier (the
#              existing substrate-altitude reference primitive);
#              realisation layer maps to host filesystem path or
#              equivalent (`~/.mirror/` on a developer machine; could
#              be `/var/spectral/`, `/srv/spectral/`, or similar on a
#              server).
type root = {
  base:   supervisor,
  anchor: ref,
}

# === start_root — root constructor ===
#
# Spawn the parentless supervisor for a given host anchor. The
# constructor establishes the self-parenting invariant: the embedded
# gen_prism's `identity` is computed (per uuid_spectral's
# autopoietic fixed point), and its `parent` field is set to that
# same identity (the self-loop that terminates the acyclic chain).
#
# The supervisor's initial child_specs are empty; children are added
# downstream through the supervisor's `start_child` (per
# shards/spectral/supervisor.mirror, commit 452ccb2). The restart
# strategy defaults to `one_for_one` (the most permissive of the
# three; matches BEAM's application-supervisor default).
#
# Body discharges as `\`; concrete construction (identity computation,
# self-parent edge establishment, default restart_strategy assignment,
# anchor binding) lives at the realisation layer via
# @code/metalogue/materialize (per the ouroboros pipeline in
# docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §5).
start_root(anchor: ref) -> root { \ }

out @spectral/root
out root
out start_root
